    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-h2-patterns",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-h2-patterns-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "2. Pattern Catalog & Formal Realizations",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-p-patterns-intro",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-p-patterns-intro-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "In this installment, we formalize the following core integration patterns established by Gregor Hohpe and Bobby Woolf, mapping each to its modern cloud-native realization:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-pat-00",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-pat-00-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Content-Based Router: Stateless dispatch engine inspecting message payload properties to route messages to appropriate destination channels.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-pat-01",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-pat-01-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Message Filter: Boundary gatekeeper evaluating criteria to discard uninteresting messages without consumer processing overhead.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-pat-02",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-pat-02-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Dynamic Router & Recipient List: Rule-driven routing where recipient channels are determined dynamically at runtime based on configuration or registry lookup.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-pat-03",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-pat-03-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Splitter: Decomposes a composite message containing multiple items into distinct independent messages for parallel processing.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-pat-04",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-pat-04-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Aggregator: Stateful mediation component that correlates and merges multiple related messages into a unified composite message.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-pat-05",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-pat-05-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Resequencer: Buffers and reorders out-of-sequence messages according to sequence metadata before downstream delivery.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-pat-06",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-pat-06-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Scatter-Gather: Broadcasts a request to multiple parallel providers and aggregates their responses within a bounded timeout deadline.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-pat-07",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-pat-07-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Routing Slip: Choreographed routing pattern where the message header carries an explicit sequence of processing steps to traverse.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-pat-08",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-pat-08-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Process Manager (Saga Coordinator): Centralized stateful orchestrator directing multi-step distributed workflows, coordinating compensating actions during failure.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-h2-invariants",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-h2-invariants-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "3. Invariants, Failure Modes & Physical Constraints",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-p-invariants-intro",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-p-invariants-intro-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Engineering resilient enterprise integration topologies requires analyzing the exact failure boundaries and physical constraints governing these patterns:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-inv-00",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-inv-00-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Aggregator Memory Saturation: Aggregators must retain partial state until completion conditions are met; missing fragments or lost messages risk memory exhaustion without bounded completion timeouts.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-inv-01",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-inv-01-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Choreography vs Orchestration: Routing Slips maximize component autonomy but obscure overall system state; Process Managers provide centralized observability and deterministic saga compensation at the expense of an orchestration bottleneck.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-03-inv-02",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-03-inv-02-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Resequencer Buffer Windowing: Sliding-window resequencing requires strict boundary sizing to prevent buffer starvation when messages are permanently dropped upstream.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    }
  ]
}